  "scope": "New 1.12.2 wireless handoff uncertainty for an exact owner, dimension and target coordinate. The fence outlives the driving tile/network and is consulted by wireless endpoint admission and autonomous item source/sink admission.",
  "contract": {
    "storage": "Per-dimension WorldSavedData; one random token per wireless handoff and an owner/target reference-count index. No loaded-world scan.",
    "ordering": "The escrow block hook marks the tile and reserves the captured target token before an executed foreign mutation. Invalid results/exceptions retain the token. Only validated settlement with empty, unblocked escrow removes that operation's token.",
    "bounds": "At most 4096 unresolved tokens per dimension. A full journal rejects a new reservation before that operation's provider mutation; no old entries are dropped.",
    "corrupt_data": "Malformed/unknown journal NBT is retained opaquely and denies target admission rather than silently losing uncertainty.",
    "removal": "Breaking/removing a quarantined tile can still produce the existing sealed receipt, but does not delete the independent world target fence.",
    "persistence_boundary": "Native fixtures round-trip NBT and save/reload the real compressed world-data file using a fresh MapStorage in the same server process. This is not a crash/restart or arbitrary user-world acceptance claim."
  },
